In my terminology conflict and polypiling are not abuses (polypiling was in
the previous version), cursed bell is one. By abuse I mean here 'massive use
of certain game features to one's advantage, leading to a serious unbalance
of the game'. Polypiling has been made more difficult and risky, and conflict
has its bad sides as you noticed - so they are not that unbalancing. Cursed
bell on the other hand leads to what you have seen: characters with thousands
HP's and power points - and this without taking any risks (as undead are
absolutely no threat to a powerful, properly equipped character) - it is just
a question of spending a few days in front of your screen doing the same again
and again...
  In other words - abuses are born where the game authors didn't think about
certain side-effects of game fetures they invented. This means that abuses
usually get plugged in the next version of the game (cf conflict and polypiling
modifications in 3.1). Hope this happens to the bell trick (that is that
it does not disappear but gets more limited and difficult/risky)
